CAT = "cpafarChanges"; SEG = "CHG"
Q = [
("A company revises the remaining useful life of its equipment. The change is applied:",
 "Prospectively, now and later", ["Retrospectively to prior years", "As a cumulative catch-up now", "As a prior-period adjustment"],
 "A change in estimate affects the current and future periods only. Prior statements are not restated."),
("A company switches from double-declining balance to straight-line depreciation. Under ASC 250 this is:",
 "Applied prospectively", ["Applied retrospectively", "A cumulative effect in income", "A prior-period adjustment"],
 "A change in depreciation method is a change in estimate effected by a change in principle, so it is applied prospectively."),
("Equipment cost $120,000 with no salvage value and a 10-year life. After 4 years the company decides the total life will be 8 years. Depreciation in year 5 is:",
 "$18,000", ["$12,000", "$15,000", "$9,000"],
 "Book value is $120,000 - $48,000 = $72,000, spread over the 4 remaining years: $18,000. $15,000 wrongly spreads the original cost over the new total life."),
("A company changes its inventory method from FIFO to weighted average cost. The change is reported by:",
 "Retrospective application", ["Prospective application", "Cumulative effect in income", "Disclosure only"],
 "A change in accounting principle is applied retrospectively to all periods presented unless it is impracticable to do so."),
("A company changes to LIFO, and it is impracticable to determine the effect on prior periods. The company:",
 "Applies LIFO prospectively", ["Restates every prior period", "Books a cumulative effect", "Delays the change a year"],
 "When the period-specific or cumulative effects cannot be determined, ASC 250 applies the new principle from the earliest date practicable, usually the start of the current year for LIFO."),
("A company finds a material error in statements it issued last year. It should:",
 "Restate the prior periods", ["Correct it in this year's income", "Disclose it without correcting", "Adjust only next year"],
 "Correcting an error in previously issued statements is a restatement: prior periods presented are corrected, and the opening retained earnings of the earliest period is adjusted."),
("A company's 2025 ending inventory was overstated by $15,000, and the error was never corrected. Ignoring taxes, 2025 net income was:",
 "Overstated by $15,000", ["Understated by $15,000", "Overstated by $30,000", "Not affected"],
 "Overstated ending inventory understates cost of goods sold, so net income is overstated by the same $15,000."),
("A company's 2025 ending inventory was overstated by $15,000, and the error was never corrected. Ignoring taxes, 2026 net income is:",
 "Understated by $15,000", ["Overstated by $15,000", "Understated by $30,000", "Not affected"],
 "The overstated 2025 ending inventory becomes overstated 2026 beginning inventory, which overstates 2026 cost of goods sold and understates 2026 income by $15,000."),
("An inventory error made at the end of 2025 was never corrected. At the end of 2026, retained earnings are:",
 "Correct, as the error reversed", ["Overstated by the error", "Understated by the error", "Misstated by twice the error"],
 "Inventory errors counterbalance: the overstatement of 2025 income is offset by the understatement of 2026 income, so retained earnings are correct after two years."),
("A lawsuit loss is probable, and the estimate ranges from $200,000 to $500,000 with no amount in the range more likely than another. The company accrues:",
 "$200,000", ["$350,000", "$500,000", "$0"],
 "ASC 450 accrues the best estimate; when no amount in the range is better than another, the minimum is accrued and the possible further loss is disclosed."),
("A loss contingency is reasonably possible and can be estimated. The company should:",
 "Disclose it, with no accrual", ["Accrue its best estimate", "Neither accrue nor disclose", "Accrue the minimum only"],
 "Accrual requires a probable loss. A reasonably possible loss is disclosed with an estimate or range, or a statement that one cannot be made."),
("A company expects to win a lawsuit against a supplier. The expected settlement is:",
 "Not recognized until realized", ["Recognized when probable", "Recognized at expected value", "Recognized in OCI when estimable"],
 "Gain contingencies are not recognized before they are realized, to avoid recognizing income too early. They may be disclosed with care not to mislead."),
("A company sold 5,000 units this year and expects 3% to need warranty repairs costing $80 each. It paid $4,000 for repairs this year. The year-end warranty liability is:",
 "$8,000", ["$12,000", "$4,000", "$16,000"],
 "Expected warranty cost is 5,000 x 3% x $80 = $12,000, all expensed this year. Less $4,000 already paid leaves an $8,000 liability."),
("A company signs a noncancelable contract to buy raw materials next year at a price that is currently fair. The contract is:",
 "Disclosed, not recorded", ["Recorded as a liability now", "Recorded as inventory now", "Left out of the statements"],
 "An unconditional purchase commitment is an executory contract. It is disclosed but not recognized unless a loss on it arises."),
("A company committed to buy goods for $100,000 under a noncancelable contract. By year-end the goods' market price has fallen to $85,000. The company:",
 "Records a $15,000 loss now", ["Discloses it only", "Records the loss on delivery", "Records an $85,000 liability"],
 "A loss on a firm purchase commitment is recognized when the market price falls below the contract price, with a liability for the $15,000."),
("After year-end but before the statements are issued, a major customer files for bankruptcy because of a decline that had already begun before year-end. The company should:",
 "Adjust the year-end allowance", ["Disclose it, with no adjustment", "Record it in the next year", "Ignore it entirely"],
 "This is a recognized subsequent event: it gives more evidence about a condition that existed at the balance sheet date, so the year-end allowance is adjusted."),
("A fire destroys a warehouse in February, after the December 31 year-end and before the statements are issued. The company should:",
 "Disclose it, with no adjustment", ["Adjust the year-end balances", "Accrue a contingent loss", "Ignore it until next year"],
 "The fire is a nonrecognized subsequent event because the condition did not exist at year-end. A material event is disclosed with its nature and an estimate of its effect."),
("A lawsuit accrued at $90,000 at year-end is settled for $120,000 before the statements are issued. The company should:",
 "Raise the accrual to $120,000", ["Keep $90,000 and disclose it", "Record $30,000 next year", "Reverse the whole accrual"],
 "The settlement confirms a condition that existed at year-end, so the liability is adjusted to the settlement amount in the year-end statements."),
("A private company that is not an SEC filer evaluates subsequent events through:",
 "The date available to be issued", ["The balance sheet date", "The date it files its tax return", "Ninety days after year-end"],
 "Under ASC 855, entities other than SEC filers evaluate through the date the statements are available to be issued and disclose that date. SEC filers use the date issued."),
("A company begins presenting consolidated statements in place of the separate statements of its group companies, a change in the reporting entity. The change is reported by:",
 "Retrospective restatement", ["Prospective application", "Cumulative effect in income", "Disclosure, no restatement"],
 "A change in reporting entity is applied retrospectively so all periods presented show the same entity."),
]
